---
layout: base.njk
title: Checklist — PNW Moths
permalink: /checklist/index.html
description: "The complete checklist of Pacific Northwest moths — every species on the site, in taxonomic sequence, filterable by state or province and by county or regional district."
---
<h1>Checklist</h1>

<p>
  Every species on the site, in taxonomic sequence rather than alphabetical order, nested under
  family, subfamily, tribe and genus. For the same list with photographs, see
  <a href="{{ '/browse/' | url }}">Browse</a>.
</p>

{#- The <noscript> is a SIBLING, not a child. This element renders into the light
   DOM (ADR 0005), so Lit's first render replaces its children and <slot> is inert
   — a fallback placed inside would be destroyed by the code meant to preserve it. -#}
<noscript>
  <p><em>Filtering by state or district needs JavaScript. The complete list is below.</em></p>
</noscript>
<pnwm-checklist-filter data-pagefind-ignore></pnwm-checklist-filter>

{#- The list is not expandable, so this markup IS the page: the filter below only
   hides rows already present. Nothing is fetched to render it, so it works with
   JavaScript off — the architecture invariant, and also what makes the page
   printable and findable with Ctrl-F, which is what the entomologists who asked
   for it actually do with a checklist.

   Only the <li> carries a slug. The ancestors are found by walking up from the
   species that matched, rather than by repeating every slug on every enclosing
   section — this page already carries ~1,250 species, and the duplicated
   attributes would have roughly doubled its transfer size for nothing. -#}
<div class="checklist">
  {% for family in checklist %}
    <section class="checklist-group">
      <h2 id="checklist-family-{{ family.name | lower }}">{{ family.name }}</h2>
      {% for subfam in family.subfamilies %}
        {#- Heading levels track effective depth, matching Browse: a null subfamily or
           tribe flattens its children up a level so the outline never skips. -#}
        <section class="checklist-group">
          {% if subfam.name %}
            <h3 id="checklist-family-{{ family.name | lower }}--subfamily-{{ subfam.name | lower }}">{{ subfam.name }}</h3>
          {% endif %}
          {% set tribeLevel = 4 if subfam.name else 3 %}
          {% for tribe in subfam.tribes %}
            <section class="checklist-group">
              {% if tribe.name %}
                <h{{ tribeLevel }} id="checklist-family-{{ family.name | lower }}{% if subfam.name %}--subfamily-{{ subfam.name | lower }}{% endif %}--tribe-{{ tribe.name | lower }}">{{ tribe.name }}</h{{ tribeLevel }}>
              {% endif %}
              {% set genusLevel = (tribeLevel + 1) if tribe.name else tribeLevel %}
              {% for genus in tribe.genera %}
                <section class="checklist-group">
                  <h{{ genusLevel }} id="checklist-family-{{ family.name | lower }}{% if subfam.name %}--subfamily-{{ subfam.name | lower }}{% endif %}{% if tribe.name %}--tribe-{{ tribe.name | lower }}{% endif %}--genus-{{ genus.genus_slug }}">{{ genus.name }}</h{{ genusLevel }}>
                  <ul class="checklist-species">
                    {% for sp in genus.species %}
                      <li data-slug="{{ sp.slug }}"><a href="{{ ('/species/' + sp.slug + '/') | url }}"><em>{{ genus.name }} {{ sp.name }}</em>{% if sp.common_name %} — {{ sp.common_name }}{% endif %}</a></li>
                    {% endfor %}
                  </ul>
                </section>
              {% endfor %}
            </section>
          {% endfor %}
        </section>
      {% endfor %}
    </section>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
